# F3F — RC Slope Soaring Gliders                   seed definition, draft
# Rule refs: FAI Sporting Code Volume F3 Soaring 2025 (F3F.x)
#
# The seventh class, and the first the notation was not designed against — see
# notation §11. Structurally the simplest in the corpus: one phase, one task,
# one flight, one metric. It is shape-identical to F3B Task C, and interesting
# only for the two things it broke (F22, F23) and the one it still cannot say.

class F3F
  name     "RC Slope Soaring Gliders"
  fai      "F3F"
  version  "FAI F3 Soaring 2025"

  param reflightAfterNPilots Number no default boundAt BeforeFlying
                                    # F3F.1.5 "after a fixed number of pilots (e.g. 5),
                                    #   pre-defined and announced by the organiser".
                                    # Declared so the CD's choice reaches the event log;
                                    # nothing reads it — notation §11 "Left open".

  finalRanking SinglePhase                                     # F3F has no fly-off

  reflight
    entitled     Replacement                                   # F3F.1.5 — the repeat replaces; no better-of provision
    others       UndefinedRequiresRuling                       # F3F.1.5 re-flies one pilot; it says nothing about the rest of the group
    minNewGroup  0                                             # F3F re-flies into the running order, not into a new group

  # F3F.1.10 is the corpus's only clause that both MULTIPLIES a penalty and
  # SUPERSEDES it with a larger one (F23). Crossings accrue per occurrence;
  # the group then keeps the largest accrued contribution, so a person contact
  # takes the whole deduction to 1000.
  penalty "safetyPlaneCrossing"     exclusionGroup "safety" perOccurrence
    deduct 100  at FinalAggregate                              # F3F.1.10 "penalised by 100 points each"
  penalty "safetyAreaObjectContact" exclusionGroup "safety"
    deduct 100  at FinalAggregate                              # F3F.1.10 "the number of contacts does not matter (maximum one penalty)"
  penalty "safetyAreaPersonContact" exclusionGroup "safety"
    deduct 1000 at FinalAggregate                              # F3F.1.10 "only 1000 points will be deducted"
  penalty "prohibitedTelemetry"
    disqualify at FinalAggregate                               # F3F.1.2 "the competitor will be disqualified from the contest"

  # ========================================================================
  phase Preliminary mandatory

    rounds    FixedSequence tasksPerRound 1                    # F3F.1.7 "the flights are to be performed round by round"; no ceiling stated
    validity  minRounds 4                                      # F3F.1.13 "a minimum of four (4) rounds must be flown"
    # Two tiers, most selective first (F22). Reversed, a 15-round contest would
    # match the >= 4 line and discard one — adoption rejects non-descending gates.
    drop      ByRound 2 whenRounds >= 15                       # F3F.1.13 "if more than fourteen (14) rounds were flown, the two (2) lowest round scores will be discarded"
    drop      ByRound 1 whenRounds >= 4                        # F3F.1.13 "in this case the lowest round score of each competitor will be discarded"

    # -- Task S — Speed --------------------------------------------------
    # The inverted task, as F3B Task C is. A raw zero is the FASTEST time in
    # the group, so every "scores zero" clause in F3F.1.6 reaches validWhen —
    # never a zero score term, and never a zeroFlight penalty effect.
    task S "Speed"                                             # F3F.1.8 ten (10) legs of a 100 m closed course
      metric    courseTime                Number s Truncate 0.01  # F3F.1.12 "the time in seconds and hundredths of seconds"
      metric    courseCompleted           Flag                 # F3F.1.6 e "the flight is not carried through"
      metric    landedInDefinedArea       Flag                 # F3F.1.6 f
      metric    launchedWithin30s         Flag                 # F3F.1.6 g "not launched within 30 seconds from the moment the starting order is given"
      metric    modelIntact               Flag                 # F3F.1.6 b "the model loses any part while airborne"
      metric    clearedPlaneWithin5s      Flag                 # F3F.1.6 h
      metric    seenEnteringCourse        Flag                 # F3F.1.6 i "not seen entering the course by the Judge at Base A"
      metric    flownWithinRules          Flag                 # F3F.1.6 a, c, d — non-conforming model, helper advice during the
                                                               #   timed flight, control by anyone other than the competitor:
                                                               #   three officials' rulings, one recorded observation
      flights   last                                           # F3F.1.5 "the competitor has one (1) attempt on each flight"
      timing    UntilAllFlightsComplete prep 180 s maxLaunches 1  # F3F.1.7 "three (3) minutes of preparation time"
      group     minPerGroup 10                                 # F3F.1.7 "at least ten (10) competitors in one group";
                                                               #   no annulment threshold is stated, so minValidResults is unset (F12)
      normalise LowerIsBetter winner 1000                      # F3F.1.12 Ri = 1000 × Tw / Ti; no precision stated (F12)
      validWhen all(courseCompleted      == true,              # F3F.1.6 — "official but gets a zero score" means NO RESULT here
                    landedInDefinedArea  == true,
                    launchedWithin30s    == true,
                    modelIntact          == true,
                    clearedPlaneWithin5s == true,
                    seenEnteringCourse   == true,
                    flownWithinRules     == true)
      score
        rate courseTime 1 pt/s                                 # the raw result IS the elapsed time; the direction inverts it

# ---- unresolved for F3F --------------------------------------------------
# Tie-break (F3F.1.13: "classification rounds" are flown until the ties are
# broken, then the discarded round's result decides) is not writable — the
# first half schedules more flying, which an ordered list of comparators cannot
# express, and the second half reads a score the drop has already removed.
# Finding F15, now open across F3B, F3K/F5K and F3F.
#
# Re-flight scheduling (F3F.1.5, "after a fixed number of pilots") has no
# ReflightRule field and no ParameterRef slot. Declared as a param above so the
# choice is recorded; it affects running order, never a score.
#
# F3F.1.10 does not say whether safety-plane crossings COMBINE with a
# safety-area object contact. It states only that the 1000-point person contact
# supersedes. Under "largest accrued contribution wins" two crossings (200)
# beat an object contact (100) and 300 is never deducted. That is a reading,
# not a rule, and wants a ruling rather than a model change.
#
# ---- confirmed non-gaps ---------------------------------------------------
# * wholeFieldAsOneGroup stays removed. F3F.1.17 evaluates the whole field as
#   one group when the weather is stable and splits only when it is not;
#   "as few groups as possible, minimum 10" already yields one group at any
#   field size, and the split is a weather ruling on the Competition, not class
#   data. Second class to test F11's removal, second to confirm it.
# * The two thirty-second windows (F3F.1.7) need no timing vocabulary: the
#   launch window is the launchedWithin30s flag, and the course-entry window
#   only moves the instant courseTime starts, which is a measurement rule.
# * Weather interruption (F3F.1.17: a group interrupted for more than thirty
#   minutes restarts from the beginning) is a group annulment and a re-draw —
#   the same ruling as F3B.1.11 c. No model gap.
